  "verify": "OFFICIAL ESPRESSIF MICRO-USB BOARD ONLY. Its 25.4×62.74 mm PCB and 22.86 mm header-row spacing do not describe dual USB-C clones. The separate VCC-GND YD-ESP32-S3 mechanical reference now has a published 27.94×57.15 mm PCB drawing and native Altium pad coordinates; see assets/geometry-evidence/variant-records.json and the full catalog record vcc-gnd:yd-esp32-s3:mechanical-reference. No exact match to Elkim/Fibel/RoboNordic seller hardware is established. Do not copy this file's coordinates, USB openings or heights to another board. This file's official drawing supports some planar geometry, but PCB thickness, component heights and LED size remain model assumptions. The antenna shape was previously clipped to 3.9 mm to satisfy a drawing validator; that is not source-backed. Independent review of the official V1.1 DXF PDF found no numerical antenna-overhang or overall assembled-length callout. The former claim of approximately 6.2 mm is therefore also unverified. This model must not be treated as a complete case-fit envelope. Measure the exact assembled board, antenna extent, fitted-header orientation and USB plug clearance before fabrication.",
  "sources": [
    "https://dl.espressif.com/dl/schematics/esp_idf/DXF_ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1_V1.1_20220429.pdf (Espressif dimension drawing, rendered and read)",
    "https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-dev-kits/en/latest/esp32s3/esp32-s3-devkitc-1/user_guide_v1.1.html (header tables J1/J3, RGB LED GPIO, octal-memory note)",
    "https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/latest/esp32/api-reference/peripherals/adc/adc_oneshot.html (ADC2 and Wi-Fi limitation)",
